{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"RCA: scheduler-sensitive fake-server pacing shared a 2s low-speed window between dribble and zero-byte-stall controls, so suite load could make valid dribble traffic look stalled. The fix keeps 2s for stall tests, uses the production 10s window for one real Git/libcurl dribble check, and makes pacing coverage deterministic. Evidence: 11 focused and 11,859 full tests passed; Gerrit 1596 merged as aab49891 after CI run 31502773813 passed."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786460850644548001,"uuid":"624b4596-2f1d-41e8-a862-1f5b5fce5560"}